10. PRIVACY
   The Software does not connect to the internet by itself and never sends
   data to the Licensor. It collects no statistics and has no telemetry.

   Discord status (optional). If the Discord desktop app runs on the same
   computer, the Software can show "Playing Jank!" on Your Discord profile.
   For this it talks only to the Discord app on Your computer (through
   Discord's local connection, not through the internet). It sends: the
   name of the current mode and a short description of what You do in it
   (for example "Editing polygons, 96 vertices"), the time since the project
   was opened, and, only if You allow it, the name of the project. The
   Discord app then shows this to other people as Discord's own terms and
   privacy policy describe; the Licensor receives nothing. You turn it on or
   off, and choose what is shown, in Settings > Discord. The name of the
   project is hidden unless You turn it on.

   If a later version adds any other feature that sends data, it will be
   described in this agreement and in the program before it is turned on.

